# Desktop web styling (ds4 chat-ui)

Local desktop web app — not mobile, not a marketing landing page. Restyle toward a **cool, atmospheric tool UI** with clear hierarchy and little chrome. Prefer CSS custom properties in `styles.css`; keep HTML structure (`shell` / `rail` / `stage` / `transcript` / `composer`) unless a layout change is required for clarity.

## Composition

- One job per region: rail = chats; stage-head = title/actions; transcript = messages; composer = input.
- Whitespace separates; do not stack nested gray boxes, thin borders on every tile, or card-in-card.
- Cards only when they hold interaction (composer, attach chips, controls). Message text should stay calm and readable — not gamified chrome.
- Atmosphere on the canvas is welcome (subtle gradients, grain, depth). Avoid flat single-color fills as the whole look.

## Surfaces & controls

- Primary actions: tangible weight via **broad radii** (~12–16px) and **offset bottom borders**, not muddy multi-layer shadows or glow.
- Press/hover: short CSS transition; optional `translateY` that collapses the offset border on `:active`.
- Group only when needed with one quiet surface — not a bento of bordered panels.
- Icons/marks: purposeful only (brand mark, attach, status). No decorative emoji chrome or icon spam.

## Tokens & type

Define roles as CSS variables (extend existing `:root` tokens; do not scatter one-off hex):

| Role | Intent |
|------|--------|
| canvas / ink | deep cool base |
| text / muted | high-contrast body + secondary |
| accent | sharp cool or warm accent (teal/amber family OK) |
| danger | semantic errors only |
| radius / fonts | shared geometry and type |

- Typography: expressive display + mono for code/meta. Prefer **weight over size jumps**.
- Do **not** default to Inter, Roboto, Arial, or bare `system-ui` stacks.

## Motion

- Prefer CSS `transition` / limited `@keyframes` for state and press feedback.
- A few intentional motions beat constant animation. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
- No infinite glow pulses, shimmer spam, or decorative particle noise that competes with reading.

## Hard avoids (AI-generic / cliché)

- Purple-on-white or purple→indigo gradient themes
- Warm cream canvas near `#F4F1EA` with terracotta + display serif
- Broadsheet look: hairline rules, zero radius, dense newspaper columns
- Soft neumorphism, heavy blur/vibrancy stacks, rounded-full pill clusters
- Generic “AI chat” glow, badge stickers, and multi-shadow card grids

## Before restyling

1. Note current hierarchy and token usage in `styles.css` / `index.html`.
2. List what to remove (borders, nested cards, redundant chrome) vs what needs weight (primary CTAs, composer).
3. Map colors to semantic variables; keep light/dark coherent if both exist.
4. Verify desktop widths (rail + stage) and readable transcript contrast.

## Checklist

```
- [ ] Regions stay single-purpose; whitespace over nested boxes
- [ ] Controls use tokenized color/radius; offset depth on primary actions
- [ ] Type pairing is distinctive; no Inter/Roboto/Arial defaults
- [ ] Atmosphere without flat-only OR glow/pill spam
- [ ] Motion is purposeful; reduced-motion honored
- [ ] Hard avoids above not introduced
```
